# The full gate before anything leaves this machine: typecheck, lint, tests.
#
# pre-push rather than pre-commit on purpose — it runs once per push instead of
# once per commit, so the ~15s lands where it is worth paying and small
# work-in-progress commits stay cheap.
#
# `npm test` alone is NOT this gate: vitest is transpile-only, so types are only
# checked by the typecheck step. See docs/TECH-DEBT.md §7.1.
#
# Genuinely need to push past a failure? `git push --no-verify`. The GitHub
# Action re-runs the same command, so it will still be caught there.
npm run check
